<article class="env-lemma" id="0571">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0571">Lemma <span data-tag="0571">37.23.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a flat morphism of schemes which is locally of finite presentation. Let $s \in S$ be a point in the image of $f$. Then there exists a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ S' \ar[rr] \ar[rd]_ g &  &  X \ar[ld]^ f \\  &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $g : S' \to S$ is flat, locally of finite presentation, locally quasi-finite, and $s \in g(S')$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The fibre $X_ s$ is not empty by assumption. Hence there exists a closed point $x \in X_ s$ where $f$ is Cohen-Macaulay, see Lemma <a href="/tag/045U" data-tag="045U">37.22.7</a>. Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0570" data-tag="0570">37.23.4</a> and set $S' = Z$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>